{
  "slug": "html_formatting",
  "course": "html",
  "order": 8,
  "url": "/html/html_formatting.asp",
  "title": "HTML Text Formatting",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "HTML Text Formatting"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "HTML contains several elements for defining text with a special meaning."
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_intro"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML Formatting Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Formatting elements were designed to display special types of text:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "<b> - Bold text",
        "<strong> - Important text",
        "<i> - Italic text",
        "<em> - Emphasized text",
        "<mark> - Marked text",
        "<small> - Smaller text",
        "<del> - Deleted text",
        "<ins> - Inserted text",
        "<sub> - Subscript text",
        "<sup> - Superscript text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <b> and <strong> Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <b> element defines bold text,\nwithout any extra importance."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<b>This text is bold</b>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_b"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <strong> element defines text\nwith strong importance. The content inside is typically displayed in bold."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<strong>This text is\n     important!</strong>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_strong"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <i> and <em> Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <i> element defines a part of\ntext in an alternate voice or mood. The content inside is typically displayed in\nitalic."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: The <i> tag is often used to indicate a technical term,\na phrase from another language, a thought, a ship name, etc."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<i>This text is italic</i>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_i"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <em> element defines\nemphasized text. The content inside is typically displayed in italic."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: A screen reader will pronounce the words in <em>\nwith an emphasis, using verbal stress."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<em>This text is\n emphasized</em>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_em"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <small> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <small> element defines\nsmaller text:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<small>This is some smaller text.</small>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_small"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <mark> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <mark> element defines text\nthat should be marked or highlighted:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>Do not forget to buy <mark>milk</mark> today.</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_mark"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <del> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <del> element defines text\nthat has been deleted from a document. Browsers will usually strike a line\nthrough deleted text:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>My favorite color is <del>blue</del> red.</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_del"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <ins> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <ins> element defines a text\nthat has been inserted into a document. Browsers will usually underline inserted\ntext:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>My favorite color is <del>blue</del> <ins>red</ins>.</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_del_ins"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <sub> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <sub> element defines\nsubscript text. Subscript text appears half a character below the normal line,\nand is sometimes rendered in a smaller font. Subscript text can be used for\nchemical formulas, like H2O:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>This\n is <sub>subscripted</sub> text.</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_sub"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML <sup> Element"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML <sup> element defines\nsuperscript text. Superscript text appears half a character above the normal\nline, and is sometimes rendered in a smaller font. Superscript text can be used\nfor footnotes, like WWW[1]:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>This\n is <sup>superscripted</sup> text.</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_sup"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML Text Formatting Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Tag", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["<b>", "Defines bold text"],
        ["<em>", "Defines emphasized text"],
        ["<i>", "Defines a part of text in an alternate voice or mood"],
        ["<small>", "Defines smaller text"],
        ["<strong>", "Defines important text"],
        ["<sub>", "Defines subscripted text"],
        ["<sup>", "Defines superscripted text"],
        ["<ins>", "Defines inserted text"],
        ["<del>", "Defines deleted text"],
        ["<mark>", "Defines marked/highlighted text"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "For a complete list of all available HTML tags, visit our HTML Tag Reference."
    }
  ]
}
